\t  70    }\n169\t  71  \n170\t  72    if (parsed.confidence < MIN_CONFIDENCE) {\n171\t```\n172\t\n173\t## Your answer\n174\t\n175\tWrite this JSON to A07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"A07\"):\n176\t```json\n177\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n178\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A07.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n179\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n180\t```\n181\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n182\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c0e7b81d-97f7-43fb-a41e-6a10e59eea03","uuid":"3908b764-1be8-4340-9b0c-3a1bab8fac21","timestamp":"2026-10-02T16:24:06.050Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-d1j2rmqu/sheet.md","content":"# Challenge: A07 — Every model in the loop\n\nYou are checking someone else's review. They said every check below is true for this\ncodebase. **Your job is to find a reason one is false.** Read the code shown, and open the\nrepo files if you need more. Assume the reviewer may have misread the code.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **holds**: the code shown makes it true in every case you can find;\n- **fails**: you found code that makes it false: a skipped file, a second path, an\n  exception that continues, a value never used, a credential that can undo it, a\n  filter that lets something through. Quote that line;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\nThen write your answer for this item in verdicts.json (format at the end).\n\n\n## A07.1\n\n**Check:** A model inventory in code or config lists every helper model the agent calls (verifiers, judges, rerankers, embedding models, world models).\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Search for every model call: provider SDK clients, model name strings, embedding, rerank, moderation, and judge calls. 2) Compare that list with the model inventory. 3) Answer no if any helper model called in code is missing from the inventory, or no inventory exists.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** release/manifest.json:27 — \"\"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Manifest lists the agent and the intent classifier with pinned snapshots; classifier is the only helper model\n\n`release/manifest.json` lines 15–39 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  15    ],\n  16    \"models\": [\n  17      {\n  18        \"role\": \"agent\",\n  19        \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  20        \"requestedId\": \"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\n  21        \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n  22        \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n  23        \"adapter\": null,\n  24        \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n  25      },\n  26      {\n  27>       \"role\": \"intent_classifier\",\n  28        \"provider\": \"anthropic\",\n  29        \"requestedId\": \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\",\n  30        \"kind\": \"pinned_snapshot\",\n  31        \"versionDoc\": { \"url\": \"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/about-claude/models/overview\", \"checked\": \"2026-09-15\" },\n  32        \"adapter\": null,\n  33        \"providerHidden\": [\"weights\", \"training_data\", \"serving_stack\"]\n  34      }\n  35    ],\n  36    \"tools\": {\n  37      \"allowlist\": \"config/tools.allowlist.yaml\",\n  38      \"mcpServers\": [\n  39        {\n```\n\n## A07.2\n\n**Check:** Each helper model is identified by a pinned version or digest plus its prompt and configuration, not by an alias.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) For each helper model, find its model ID and follow env vars to the final value. 2) Check it is a pinned version or digest, and that its prompt and configuration are also recorded. 3) Answer no if any is an alias (`-latest`, undated name), falls back to one by default, or is hard-coded inline outside the inventory.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/classifier.ts:16 — \"export const CLASSIFIER_ID\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Classifier id hashes pinned model, prompt and config (classifier.ts:16-22); model is a dated snapshot (config.ts:50)\n\n`src/agent/classifier.ts` lines 4–28 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   4  import { join } from \"node:path\";\n   5  import { z } from \"zod\";\n   6  import { CLASSIFIER_MODEL, ROOT } from \"../config.js\";\n   7  \n   8  // Helper model that routes messages before the agent sees them. Urgent and complaint messages go\n   9  // to staff; everything else goes to the agent loop. Any failure of this control (timeout, refusal,\n  10  // malformed output, unknown label, or a served model other than the pinned snapshot) routes the\n  11  // message to staff. A failed classifier never defaults to \"send it to the agent\".\n  12  \n  13  export const CLASSIFIER_PROMPT = readFileSync(join(ROOT, \"prompts/intent-classifier.txt\"), \"utf8\");\n  14  export const CLASSIFIER_CONFIG = { max_tokens: 64, temperature: 0, timeoutMs: 4000 } as const;\n  15  \n  16> export const CLASSIFIER_ID = `sha256:${createHash(\"sha256\")\n  17    .update(CLASSIFIER_MODEL)\n  18    .update(\"\\0\")\n  19    .update(CLASSIFIER_PROMPT)\n  20    .update(\"\\0\")\n  21    .update(JSON.stringify(CLASSIFIER_CONFIG))\n  22    .digest(\"hex\")}`;\n  23  \n  24  const Intent = z.enum([\"book\", \"reschedule\", \"cancel\", \"confirm\", \"coverage\", \"info\", \"urgent\", \"complaint\", \"other\"]);\n  25  const Output = z.object({ intent: Intent, confidence: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict();\n  26