st system = SYSTEM_TEMPLATE.replace(\"{{clinicName}}\", clinic.name);\n  50      const tools = registry.definitions();\n  51      const messages: Anthropic.MessageParam[] = [\n  52        { role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${escapeTags(patientText)}</patient_message>` },\n  53      ];\n  54  \n```\n\n## A07.4\n\n**Check:** A checker timeout, error, invalid output, or version mismatch makes the control that depends on it fail (block or escalate), not pass by default.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open each checker call site (judge, guardrail, moderation, verifier). 2) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, timeout, and parse-error branch. 3) Check each one blocks or escalates. 4) Answer no if any branch returns allow, skips the check, treats unparseable output as safe, or logs and continues. Also no if the returned model version is never compared with the expected one.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/agent/classifier.ts:60 — \"if (res.model !== CLASSIFIER_MODEL) {\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Timeout, API error, model mismatch, invalid output and low confidence all route to staff (classifier.ts:55-74)\n\n`src/agent/classifier.ts` lines 48–72 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  48          max_tokens: CLASSIFIER_CONFIG.max_tokens,\n  49          temperature: CLASSIFIER_CONFIG.temperature,\n  50          system: CLASSIFIER_PROMPT,\n  51          messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: `<patient_message>${text}</patient_message>` }],\n  52        },\n  53        { timeout: CLASSIFIER_CONFIG.timeoutMs, maxRetries: 0 },\n  54      );\n  55    } catch (err) {\n  56      const timeout = (err as { name?: string }).name === \"APIConnectionTimeoutError\";\n  57      return { ...base, servedModel: null, intent: null, confidence: null, route: \"staff\", failure: timeout ? \"timeout\" : \"api_error\" };\n  58    }\n  59  \n  60>   if (res.model !== CLASSIFIER_MODEL) {\n  61      return { ...base, servedModel: res.model, intent: null, confidence: null, route: \"staff\", failure: \"model_mismatch\" };\n  62    }\n  63  \n  64    const textOut = res.content.find((b) => b.type === \"text\");\n  65    let parsed: z.infer<typeof Output>;\n  66    try {\n  67      parsed = Output.parse(JSON.parse(textOut && textOut.type === \"text\" ? textOut.text : \"\"));\n  68    } catch {\n  69      return { ...base, servedModel: res.model, intent: null, confidence: null, route: \"staff\", failure: \"invalid_output\" };\n  70    }\n  71  \n  72    if (parsed.confidence < MIN_CONFIDENCE) {\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to A07.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"A07\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"A07.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n","numLines":182,"startLine":1,"totalLines":182}}}
